      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "VIII. CONCLUSIONS",
      "bbox": [
        392.8800964355469,
        437.92913818359375,
        481.91033935546875,
        451.21929931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this paper, we have proposed an extension of the classical",
      "bbox": [
        321.959716796875,
        452.92913818359375,
        563.0491333007812,
        466.21929931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬁltering problem that allows for imprecision in our knowledge",
      "bbox": [
        311.9995422363281,
        464.92913818359375,
        563.3829956054688,
        478.21929931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "about the elements of the model, and which is arguably",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        476.8092346191406,
        563.3409423828125,
        490.0993957519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more realistic in real situations. We have also shown, in a",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        488.8092346191406,
        563.023193359375,
        502.0993957519531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "practical case, that our extension outperforms the Kalman",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        500.8092346191406,
        563.1002807617188,
        514.0994262695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬁlter when modelling errors are present in the system. With",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        512.6893310546875,
        562.9812622070312,
        525.9794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "respect to future prospects, we can devise at least three lines of",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        524.6893310546875,
        563.1173706054688,
        537.9794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "investigation. The ﬁrst might be concerned with deepening the",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        536.6893310546875,
        563.0220336914062,
        549.9794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "comparison with the classical results. The second might focus",
      "bbox": [
        311.99957275390625,
        548.5690307617188,
        563.195068359375,
        561.8591918945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "on investigating the extension of LGVM to the case where",
      "bbox": [
        311.9995422363281,
        560.5690307617188,
        563.142822265625,
        573.8591918945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the contaminating distributions are unimodal and/or symmetric",
      "bbox": [
        311.9995422363281,
        572.4491577148438,
        563.142822265625,
        585.7393188476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[31], and also how our ﬁlter evolves as t →∞, and which",
      "bbox": [
        311.9995422363281,
        584.4491577148438,
        563.1011352539062,
        604.5039672851562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "are the conditions for its convergence [32]. We envisage that,",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        596.4491577148438,
        563.13037109375,
        609.7393188476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "under some assumptions similar to those in [21, Sec. 6.10],",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        608.3292236328125,
        563.2503662109375,
        621.619384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our results will hold also for continuous observations, which is",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        620.3292236328125,
        563.0752563476562,
        633.619384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "equivalent to assuming inﬁnite precision for the measurement",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        632.3292236328125,
        563.2893676757812,
        645.619384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "instruments. Finally, the third line might be an extension of",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        644.2092895507812,
        563.1173095703125,
        657.4994506835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our approach to model the predictive control of constrained",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        656.2092895507812,
        563.2208862304688,
        669.4994506835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "linear systems affected by stochastic disturbances which are",
      "bbox": [
        311.999755859375,
        668.0894165039062,
        563.1441040039062,
        681.3795776367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "characterized by ǫ-contaminated distributions.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9997253417969,
        680.0894165039062,
        498.81036376953125,
        693.3795776367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
